---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: a recipient that needs a physical interaction cannot be the
primary one.

Decrypting to age1yubikey1qqqqqqqq...
requires the card present, a PIN and a touch, once per file. Activation
decrypts non-interactively, with the identity sops.age.sshKeyPaths
names, so a profile whose only recipient is a hardware key cannot
activate at all — and the failure lands at switch time on their
machine, not here.

A card belongs in the same person's recoveryRecipients, which is
additive: every file their audience names is encrypted to it as well as
to recipient, so the card opens their files after the activation key is
lost and is needed at no other time.

Pass their software recipient here, then add the card by hand.
